<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Amir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1061</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a> ibn Abi Amir, a grandson of the Córdoban regent al-Mansur, ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> from 1021 to 1061. He was recognised by the city after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> and for a time also held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a>. His family, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amirids">Amirids</a>, kept Valencia until 1065, when it passed to the taifa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a>.</p></div>
